y":["BNY (Bank of New York Mellon) is the largest custody bank, holding and servicing assets for investors, and also runs Pershing and wealth management. Revenue (net interest income plus noninterest income) rose 7.8% to $20.1B in 2025. Net interest income rose 14.7% to $4.9B and noninterest income rose 5.8% to $15.1B; noninterest expense rose 3.5%, and the provision for credit losses was −$32.0M, versus $70.0M.","Net income to common rose 22.4% to $5.3B, or $7.40 per diluted share, and the efficiency ratio was 64.3% versus 67.0%. BNY returned $5.0B through dividends and buybacks."],"highlights":["Revenue rose 7.8% to $20.1B.","Net interest income rose 14.7%.","Noninterest income rose 5.8%.","Net income to common rose 22.4% to $5.3B."],"watch":["Net interest income depends on interest rates.","Noninterest expense was $12.9B, up 3.5%.","Credit-loss reserves were released ($32.0M)."],"table":[["Total revenue",20.08,18.619,1],["Net interest income",4.944,4.312],["Noninterest income",15.136,14.307],["Noninterest expense",12.912,12.48],["Provision for credit losses",-0.032,0.07],["Other items, net",-0.142,-0.221],["Pre-tax income",7.058,5.848,1],["Income tax",1.475,1.305],["Noncontrolling interests",-0.034,-0.013],["Preferred dividends & other",-0.243,0.194],["Net income to common",5.306,4.336,1],["Diluted EPS ($)",7.4,5.8,0,"eps"],["Book value per share ($)",57.359656,51.520156,0,"eps"]],"sources":[["The Bank of New York Mellon Corporation Form 10-K filings (SEC EDGAR)","https://www.sec.gov/cgi-bin/browse-edgar?action=getcompany&CIK=0001390777&type=10-K"],["BNY financial statements (StockAnalysis)","https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/bny/financials/"]]},"video":{"revenueLine":{"cap":"Net interest income was 25% of revenue.","say":"Net interest income made up 25 percent of revenue."},"spotlights":[{"kicker":"Revenue","big":"$20.1B","sub":"revenue · +7.8%","lines":["Net interest income $4.9B","Noninterest income $15.1B"],"cap":"Revenue rose 7.8% to $20.1B.","say":"Revenue r